From: nura-builds
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: COMMAND_LINE_SIZE 2048

Samsung's msm8226 bootloader appends about 840 characters of its own and
refuses to boot a command line over 1024 bytes in total, so the device
options are built in (CONFIG_CMDLINE, CONFIG_CMDLINE_EXTEND); appended
after the bootloader's line they need a buffer larger than 1024.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/setup.h b/arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/setup.h
index 8e50e03..11b9f8f 100644
--- a/arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/setup.h
+++ b/arch/arm/include/uapi/asm/setup.h
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 
 #include <linux/types.h>
 
-#define COMMAND_LINE_SIZE 1024
+#define COMMAND_LINE_SIZE 2048
 
 /* The list ends with an ATAG_NONE node. */
 #define ATAG_NONE	0x00000000
